## Decision
The UI link now carries a single-use nonce. When the link is opened, the nonce is exchanged for a session, and the browser cookie holds a separate session secret. This way, a leaked or logged URL (browser history, referrer headers, shell output) cannot be replayed after first use. The cookie value never appears in a URL, so the two credentials are kept apart.

